====================================================================================================
  [PASS] 3a at fixed local field w the deep-MOND phantom is sqrt(a0) w / (4 pi G sqrt(G M)): it still depends on M, so no function eps(w) of the local field alone reproduces it for two masses (d eps/d M != 0)
           (eps(w, M) = sqrt(a0)*w/(4*pi*G**(3/2)*sqrt(M)))
  [PASS] 3b the same statement is certified in Lean (lean_2026/SW06_local_nogo.lean: local_nogo, epsMOND_rewrite; compiled exit 0, axioms propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound only -- see lean_2026/SW06_local_nogo.out)
    READING: a shared-metric phantom needs a SOURCED Poisson-type equation (QUMOND/AQUAL's div[mu grad phi] = 4 pi G rho). Sourcing by matter directly makes the field act
    on matter (a fifth force photons do not feel: horn C again); sourcing through the metric needs a second field carrying the constraint -- AeST's vector, whose tie
    to the MOND scalar fixes alpha1 = -2(K_B + 2) (record, 08-31). The record's LOCAL no-go theorem (fried-chicken) is the same statement at the level of the force law.

